WEBVTT

00:05.007 --> 00:07.677
[Rudeus panting]

00:09.597 --> 00:10.767
-[ZANOBA] Master!
-[gasps]

00:10.847 --> 00:12.477
[yelling]

00:12.557 --> 00:15.977
-[gasps]
-[Elinalise, Cliff screaming]

00:16.067 --> 00:18.147
[Rudeus breathing heavily]

00:18.237 --> 00:19.237
[gasps]

00:22.697 --> 00:26.157
[gasping, grunting]

00:27.247 --> 00:30.957
[screaming]

00:31.037 --> 00:32.167
[gasps]

00:40.417 --> 00:42.507
If Perugius hadn't shown up
when he did,

00:42.587 --> 00:44.507
I might never
have held her again.

00:45.097 --> 00:46.677
I would have lost all of them.

00:47.517 --> 00:48.557
[gasps softly]

00:49.427 --> 00:51.807
Rudy, what's wrong?

00:51.887 --> 00:53.807
[Rudeus whimpers]

00:55.057 --> 00:56.067
[SYLPHIETTE] You're safe now.

01:00.697 --> 01:02.657
[♪ opening theme song playing]

01:07.867 --> 01:09.537
-Zanoba.
-Huh?

01:09.617 --> 01:10.537
Good morning!

01:11.457 --> 01:13.457
How have your injuries healed,
Master?

01:13.537 --> 01:14.577
Fine.

01:14.667 --> 01:16.537
How about you? Yours were worse.

01:16.627 --> 01:17.957
I'm quite all right.

01:18.627 --> 01:20.007
Good, glad to hear it.

01:20.087 --> 01:21.717
Sorry my spell got you.

01:21.797 --> 01:24.927
Oh, I trust that you did
what you thought was best.

01:25.007 --> 01:26.137
Worry not.

01:26.217 --> 01:28.557
Let us instead celebrate
our safe return.

01:29.097 --> 01:30.017
Let's.

01:30.767 --> 01:31.847
If Nanahoshi gets better,

01:31.927 --> 01:33.847
we can call this
a roaring success.

01:33.937 --> 01:35.647
[CLIFF] Nanahoshi is just fine.

01:36.267 --> 01:38.607
Her condition has pretty much
stabilized by now.

01:39.187 --> 01:40.227
If we're being honest,

01:40.317 --> 01:42.527
I'm more worried
about sweet Cliff.

01:42.607 --> 01:44.817
[RUDEUS] Is it the demon eye
you got from Kishirika?

01:44.907 --> 01:48.157
Yeah. She said it's called
the Eye of Discernment.

01:49.367 --> 01:52.077
It shows me information
about everything I see.

01:52.157 --> 01:54.667
It's like the whole world
is flooded with text.

01:54.747 --> 01:56.837
Yeah,
I ran into a similar problem

01:56.917 --> 01:58.707
right after I got my demon eye.

01:58.787 --> 02:01.757
Well, I'll get it
under control soon.

02:01.837 --> 02:04.047
If we run into anything else
like Dryne Syndrome,

02:04.127 --> 02:05.507
you can count on me.

02:06.217 --> 02:08.507
-[RUDEUS] Thanks, Cliff.
-And if you want to visit her,

02:08.597 --> 02:09.757
now might be the time.

02:10.557 --> 02:12.227
She was still awake when I left.

02:12.307 --> 02:14.637
Great. Think I will.

02:34.247 --> 02:36.037
So, has that been helping?

02:36.117 --> 02:38.207
Yes, I'm feeling
quite a bit better.

02:38.747 --> 02:41.507
They did tell me I should spend
another month or so on bed rest,

02:41.587 --> 02:42.877
but otherwise...

02:43.507 --> 02:46.757
And thank you,
for everything you did for me.

02:48.637 --> 02:50.887
I heard you and the others
shouldered a great deal of risk

02:50.967 --> 02:52.637
to go and fetch
these tea leaves.

02:52.717 --> 02:55.597
So I appreciate it.

02:56.307 --> 02:58.267
[RUDEUS]
She's sure on her best behavior.

02:58.347 --> 02:59.767
Happy to do it.

03:00.687 --> 03:02.147
In retrospect,

03:02.227 --> 03:04.737
I've been awfully cavalier
with you ever since we met,

03:04.817 --> 03:07.067
even though you're
certainly older than me.

03:07.157 --> 03:08.447
I'm sorry about that.

03:08.527 --> 03:10.157
I don't mind at all.

03:10.237 --> 03:12.117
I'm only 18 here,
so don't sweat it.

03:12.197 --> 03:14.497
May I ask
how old you were previously?

03:14.577 --> 03:16.997
30-something?

03:17.077 --> 03:18.787
But let's not talk about that.

03:19.377 --> 03:21.037
You don't have to be so formal.

03:21.127 --> 03:22.837
Let's talk as we always have.

03:22.917 --> 03:23.957
All right.

03:28.757 --> 03:31.467
You may already know,
but the Dryne Syndrome--

03:31.547 --> 03:32.847
Is chronic.

03:32.927 --> 03:34.177
They told me so.

03:36.347 --> 03:38.637
[RUDEUS] The sokas tea can
purge the mana from her body,

03:38.727 --> 03:40.857
but it will
eventually build up again.

03:40.937 --> 03:43.647
She'll have to drink it
every day from now on.

03:43.727 --> 03:46.187
You can't avoid mana
in this world.

03:46.277 --> 03:47.527
It's in everything.

03:47.607 --> 03:48.697
It's in the air.

03:50.657 --> 03:53.537
I swear, we will find a way
to get you home.

03:54.037 --> 03:55.787
You shouldn't have to die
in this world.

03:55.867 --> 03:56.787
[gasps]

03:57.747 --> 03:58.867
Yeah.

03:58.957 --> 04:00.997
I'll do whatever I can
to make it happen.

04:02.787 --> 04:05.007
[crying]

04:05.757 --> 04:06.837
Thank you.

04:06.917 --> 04:08.167
[♪ gentle music playing]

04:09.177 --> 04:10.887
Thank you very much, Rudeus.

04:14.307 --> 04:15.507
But then, if...

04:15.597 --> 04:16.717
if I make it home...

04:16.807 --> 04:18.017
You will.

04:18.637 --> 04:20.637
I bet you can't wait
to get back.

04:20.727 --> 04:22.147
No, I mean,

04:22.647 --> 04:24.767
I won't be able
to repay all I owe you.

04:24.857 --> 04:27.317
Just forget about
owing me anything.

04:27.397 --> 04:29.777
Though, I'll always
appreciate your advice,

04:29.857 --> 04:31.407
long as you're
still hanging around.

04:32.527 --> 04:33.407
You got it.

04:36.287 --> 04:37.947
I'll let you get some rest.

04:38.037 --> 04:39.037
Glad you're better.

04:39.787 --> 04:40.827
Same.

04:40.917 --> 04:42.247
Thanks again, Rudeus.

04:44.497 --> 04:47.837
Then my master unleashed
a violent and crackling spell!

04:47.917 --> 04:50.547
It scorched her body
and paralyzed her in place.

04:50.627 --> 04:51.757
Oh?

04:51.837 --> 04:53.007
Then it was his arts

04:53.087 --> 04:55.807
that left Atofe
in such a pathetic state.

04:55.887 --> 04:58.467
Go on! I'm curious
about what happened next.

04:58.557 --> 05:00.057
Well, unfortunately,

05:00.137 --> 05:02.347
at that point
I had lost consciousness.

05:02.897 --> 05:04.227
[RUDEUS]
Hey, we having a tea party?

05:04.307 --> 05:05.477
Indeed we are!

05:05.567 --> 05:06.767
Excellent timing.

05:06.857 --> 05:08.987
Lord Perugius
expressed an interest

05:09.067 --> 05:11.067
in how our battle
with Atofe transpired,

05:11.147 --> 05:14.117
so I was just regaling him
with all the finer details.

05:14.697 --> 05:16.327
[PERUGIUS]
I'm impressed, Rudeus.

05:16.407 --> 05:18.497
Zanoba tells me
it was your magic

05:18.577 --> 05:21.497
that incapacitated
that so-called Demon King.

05:21.577 --> 05:22.787
[chuckles]

05:23.167 --> 05:25.827
Bloodied and broken is better
than that wretch deserves.

05:25.917 --> 05:28.297
[RUDEUS] Does he hate
her guts that badly?

05:28.837 --> 05:30.167
You seem pleased.

05:30.257 --> 05:32.967
It's not every day
that such a golden opportunity

05:33.047 --> 05:35.717
for vengeance falls
squarely in my lap.

05:35.797 --> 05:37.137
[RUDEUS] Vengeance, sire?

05:37.757 --> 05:38.757
Indeed.

05:39.137 --> 05:41.807
I sustained my fair share
of injuries from her

05:41.887 --> 05:43.557
during the Laplace War.

05:43.637 --> 05:46.227
I had hoped
to settle the score one day.

05:46.307 --> 05:48.817
But then,
North God Kalman married her,

05:48.897 --> 05:50.937
and on his deathbed,
made us swear

05:51.027 --> 05:52.567
we wouldn't kill each other.

05:52.647 --> 05:54.447
It shattered
my hopes of exacting

05:54.527 --> 05:56.737
any true revenge against her,

05:57.367 --> 06:00.497
but how fortuitous,
we could strike a blow together.

06:01.117 --> 06:03.577
I must thank you
for your part in this.

06:03.657 --> 06:05.457
Splendid job.

06:05.537 --> 06:07.207
And you don't mind
breaking your oath

06:07.287 --> 06:08.417
to North God Kalman?

06:08.837 --> 06:11.007
[PERUGIUS]
Kal forbade mortal combat.

06:11.087 --> 06:14.007
I'm sure he wouldn't object
to a one-sided beating.

06:14.087 --> 06:17.887
Besides, it would take far more
than that to kill that beast.

06:17.967 --> 06:19.507
[chuckles]

06:19.597 --> 06:21.887
It appears
I may have misjudged you,

06:21.967 --> 06:23.267
Master Rudeus.

06:23.637 --> 06:24.847
My apologies.

06:24.937 --> 06:26.767
I must reward you somehow.

06:26.857 --> 06:27.977
Must you?

06:28.477 --> 06:29.397
Mm.

06:30.897 --> 06:33.487
Well then,
would you be willing to impart

06:33.567 --> 06:36.357
some of your more advanced
combat techniques, my lord?

06:36.987 --> 06:40.367
[scoffs] Was it Atofe
who sparked this within you?

06:40.447 --> 06:42.367
Or do you always lust for power?

06:42.447 --> 06:44.037
No, nothing like that.

06:44.497 --> 06:46.287
My highest priority
is making sure

06:46.367 --> 06:47.877
that I can keep my family safe.

06:49.957 --> 06:51.127
Very well.

06:51.417 --> 06:53.757
Then I will provide you
with a means to contact me.

06:54.337 --> 06:55.377
Sylvaril.

06:58.507 --> 07:01.967
You may use that in any place
I have a connection to.

07:02.057 --> 07:05.727
Clearnight will hear it,
and Almanfi will come for you.

07:07.437 --> 07:09.267
[RUDEUS] Is the idea
that he'll just bail me out

07:09.357 --> 07:10.727
when I need him to?

07:10.817 --> 07:13.107
Now please, sit and join us.

07:13.187 --> 07:16.027
Surely there is more
to be said between us.

07:16.897 --> 07:18.277
[RUDEUS]
Perugius actually turned out

07:18.367 --> 07:20.737
to be a pretty cool guy once you
got to chatting with him.

07:21.777 --> 07:23.537
Of course, a lot of the things
he talked about

07:23.617 --> 07:25.287
went right over my head, but...

07:26.037 --> 07:28.497
even just getting to listen in
was fascinating.

07:29.377 --> 07:30.957
Incidentally,

07:31.037 --> 07:33.707
we've considered putting
some of my master's figurines

07:33.797 --> 07:35.457
on the market
in the near future.

07:35.547 --> 07:37.927
Would you give us the benefit
of your frank opinion?

07:38.677 --> 07:40.047
Hmm?

07:40.137 --> 07:41.677
It's a Superd.

07:41.757 --> 07:44.557
You present me with this,
knowing my hatred of demonkind?

07:44.637 --> 07:46.477
Yes, I should have known
you would have been able

07:46.557 --> 07:48.227
to recognize it
at a glance, sire.

07:49.057 --> 07:51.937
[RUDEUS] Zanoba should know
Perugius can't stand demons.

07:52.017 --> 07:53.477
He made it pretty clear.

07:53.567 --> 07:54.937
What's his angle?

07:55.027 --> 07:57.397
You would attempt
to sell a thing like this?

07:57.897 --> 07:58.817
Foolish.

07:59.567 --> 08:01.067
If you look again, my liege,

08:01.157 --> 08:02.527
you'll see
that the model of this piece

08:02.617 --> 08:05.157
is someone to whom
you owe a tremendous debt.

08:05.247 --> 08:06.327
[PERUGIUS] Indeed?

08:07.577 --> 08:08.997
Hmm.

08:09.077 --> 08:10.077
Huh.

08:10.537 --> 08:12.127
Well, as I live and breathe.

08:12.207 --> 08:13.837
Ruijerd Superdia.

08:13.917 --> 08:16.167
Precisely, sir, the very same.

08:16.257 --> 08:19.547
You quite graciously recounted
your final battle with Laplace,

08:20.337 --> 08:22.847
which is how I know
that it was this Ruijerd fellow

08:22.927 --> 08:25.427
who came to the aid of you
and your companions.

08:26.057 --> 08:27.347
Naturally, Lord Perugius,

08:27.427 --> 08:29.477
I'm well aware
of your distaste for demonkind,

08:29.557 --> 08:31.647
but consider for a moment
the greater picture.

08:31.727 --> 08:34.647
I believe that if my master's
skills had some public exposure,

08:34.727 --> 08:37.937
this type of craftsmanship
would take the world by storm.

08:38.027 --> 08:39.187
Would that not be a sight?

08:39.487 --> 08:43.027
Imagine. A world awash
with wonderful works of art!

08:43.117 --> 08:45.197
I detest the Superd.

08:45.657 --> 08:48.247
They slaughtered the innocent
without exception.

08:48.617 --> 08:51.667
Now, it is true
that if not for Ruijerd,

08:51.747 --> 08:53.377
I wouldn't be here today.

08:54.037 --> 08:56.497
However... hmm.

08:57.547 --> 08:58.627
Lord Perugius,

08:58.717 --> 09:00.717
Ruijerd carries
a great deal of regret

09:00.797 --> 09:01.887
for what he did during the war.

09:02.467 --> 09:03.887
That so?

09:03.967 --> 09:05.597
Laplace manipulated him.

09:06.007 --> 09:08.347
He tricked him
into killing his own family,

09:08.427 --> 09:10.267
into dishonoring his clan.

09:10.347 --> 09:12.437
Laplace, eh?

09:12.517 --> 09:14.397
[RUDEUS] He despises Laplace.

09:14.477 --> 09:15.727
Right now,
he's traveling the world

09:15.807 --> 09:17.817
to try and restore
his people's good name.

09:18.437 --> 09:20.147
These figures
are the least we can do

09:20.237 --> 09:21.527
to aid him in that quest.

09:22.147 --> 09:24.777
For Ruijerd's sake,
please give us your blessing.

09:25.527 --> 09:27.277
The plight of the Superd race

09:27.367 --> 09:29.617
does nothing to tug
at my heartstrings.

09:30.207 --> 09:33.207
However, I must repay my debts.

09:33.287 --> 09:35.417
[Zanoba gasps] You mean...

09:35.497 --> 09:37.537
You may do as you like.

09:37.627 --> 09:39.457
[RUDEUS]
Thank you for your kindness.

09:40.167 --> 09:41.507
And that's one more step

09:41.587 --> 09:44.547
towards rehabilitating
the Superd's reputation.

09:44.637 --> 09:47.137
Hang in there, buddy.
We're getting closer.

09:47.217 --> 09:49.427
Master, as long as
we're on the subject,

09:49.517 --> 09:50.927
why don't you give Lord Perugius

09:51.017 --> 09:52.597
a little demonstration
of your skill?

09:53.227 --> 09:54.517
With the figurines?

09:54.597 --> 09:55.937
[PERUGIUS] Yes, show me.

09:56.017 --> 09:58.067
Your magic intrigues me.

09:58.647 --> 09:59.977
Sure. Right away.

10:02.817 --> 10:05.237
You've fashioned Sylvaril?

10:05.317 --> 10:09.027
Fascinating, and a novel use
of Earth magic, indeed.

10:09.117 --> 10:10.327
Well managed.

10:10.407 --> 10:12.367
I would be happy
to make anything

10:12.457 --> 10:13.497
you'd care to commission.

10:13.577 --> 10:15.247
Will you, now?

10:15.327 --> 10:17.917
Next time you make
something of quality,

10:17.997 --> 10:19.747
bring it here and I will buy it.

10:19.837 --> 10:21.167
You like stonework?

10:21.257 --> 10:22.757
The Asura Kingdom is home

10:22.837 --> 10:25.427
to a wealth of fine
stonemasons and craftspeople.

10:26.177 --> 10:27.297
When I ascend the throne,

10:27.597 --> 10:30.097
I will happily have a statue
made in your honor.

10:30.177 --> 10:31.517
[scoffs]

10:31.597 --> 10:35.017
Statuary made to satisfy
the vanity of the nobility

10:35.097 --> 10:37.147
-should not be considered art.
-[Ariel gasps nervously]

10:37.807 --> 10:39.607
If you ascend the throne,

10:39.687 --> 10:42.277
surely you will have
more pressing concerns.

10:42.357 --> 10:43.817
Well, perhaps.

10:46.527 --> 10:48.617
[PERUGIUS] Ariel Anemoi Asura,

10:48.697 --> 10:51.617
what does a "true king" signify?

10:51.697 --> 10:54.707
Or better still,
what must a king possess?

10:54.787 --> 10:56.157
Oh, well,

10:56.787 --> 10:58.287
they should be educated,

10:58.377 --> 11:00.087
wise enough
to heed their ministers

11:00.167 --> 11:02.047
and understand the gravity
of their station--

11:02.127 --> 11:03.717
-I beg to differ.
-[gasps]

11:03.797 --> 11:06.587
My old friend
Gaunis Freean Asura

11:06.677 --> 11:07.887
was a true king,

11:07.967 --> 11:10.007
but he was nothing like that.

11:10.507 --> 11:13.267
He was cowardly
and quite adverse to battle,

11:13.347 --> 11:15.637
fond of ogling barmaids,

11:15.727 --> 11:17.727
and he was a damned fool.

11:18.347 --> 11:19.647
But still, he possessed

11:19.727 --> 11:22.437
the single most
important quality of a king.

11:22.897 --> 11:24.237
And for that,

11:24.317 --> 11:27.777
I consider him the truest ruler
your kingdom has had.

11:28.567 --> 11:30.277
What is this vital quality?

11:30.367 --> 11:32.947
If you can bring me
that answer yourself,

11:33.037 --> 11:35.497
then I will be glad
to lend you my aid.

11:36.407 --> 11:37.497
[RUDEUS] I get it.

11:37.577 --> 11:39.037
He's testing her.

11:40.167 --> 11:42.917
[PERUGIUS] Rudeus,
do you know what it is?

11:43.497 --> 11:45.087
I-I don't know, sir.

11:45.167 --> 11:46.167
But, uh...

11:47.047 --> 11:48.047
Mmm.

11:48.507 --> 11:49.797
Personally,

11:50.927 --> 11:53.347
I would much prefer a king
who can put themselves

11:53.427 --> 11:54.767
in their subjects' position.

11:54.847 --> 11:56.137
Someone of the people.

11:56.227 --> 11:57.387
Oh?

11:58.387 --> 12:01.977
This young man gave me a far
better answer than you did.

12:02.057 --> 12:03.107
[stands up]

12:03.187 --> 12:05.147
I will take my leave.

12:05.237 --> 12:07.527
But consider it well, Princess.

12:12.077 --> 12:13.237
Yes, my lord.

12:13.867 --> 12:16.077
The quality
that makes a true king.

12:17.747 --> 12:18.957
[floorboards creaking]

12:19.037 --> 12:19.957
[door opens]

12:20.747 --> 12:21.997
[SYLPHIETTE] We're back.

12:22.087 --> 12:23.417
[AISHA] Coming!

12:23.497 --> 12:24.667
Welcome home!

12:25.707 --> 12:27.007
Big Brother!

12:27.087 --> 12:28.087
Sylphie!

12:28.167 --> 12:29.087
In the flesh.

12:29.167 --> 12:30.837
So, is it over now?

12:31.387 --> 12:33.507
Were you able to save Nanahoshi?

12:33.927 --> 12:34.927
Or is she--

12:35.007 --> 12:36.637
[ROXY] Good to see you,
both of you.

12:37.387 --> 12:38.387
[SYLPHIETTE] Same to you.

12:38.477 --> 12:40.347
Are you feeling
all right, Sylphie?

12:40.437 --> 12:42.227
-Relieved?
-[SYLPHIETTE] Yup.

12:42.307 --> 12:44.607
Sorry for leaving you
to hold down the fort.

12:44.687 --> 12:46.067
Oh, I don't mind.

12:46.147 --> 12:47.317
You're too kind.

12:47.397 --> 12:48.737
This wasn't our plan.

12:48.817 --> 12:50.357
My stay got extended.

12:51.027 --> 12:52.657
Well, you're home now.

12:52.737 --> 12:54.157
I guess it worked out, then?

12:54.617 --> 12:57.327
[RUDEUS] Yeah. I'll fill you in
a bit more later.

12:57.407 --> 12:59.247
But first, your souvenir.

13:01.747 --> 13:02.997
I missed you.

13:03.077 --> 13:03.997
[gasps]

13:04.837 --> 13:06.087
Glad you're back.

13:09.837 --> 13:12.797
And so,
Nanahoshi will be fine for now.

13:13.547 --> 13:15.507
We did ask about Mom too.

13:16.047 --> 13:18.767
All we found out is
that it's a curse, most likely.

13:19.227 --> 13:20.227
Sorry.

13:20.727 --> 13:23.187
Knowing it's a curse is better
than knowing nothing.

13:23.807 --> 13:26.567
That's true,
but I'd still like to go back.

13:26.647 --> 13:28.397
Someone might know of a remedy.

13:28.937 --> 13:31.777
Yes, and I'll be away
guarding Princess Ariel

13:31.857 --> 13:33.067
for a bit, as well.

13:33.157 --> 13:34.697
I understand.

13:34.777 --> 13:36.657
We'll take care
of things here at home.

13:37.277 --> 13:38.367
Thank you.

13:38.447 --> 13:40.997
I'll try to come home
as often as I can.

13:41.077 --> 13:42.537
Please keep Lucie safe.

13:43.117 --> 13:44.077
We will.

13:44.167 --> 13:45.787
I'll make sure of it.

13:46.247 --> 13:47.417
Thanks so much.

13:49.257 --> 13:50.507
And that's my report.

13:51.047 --> 13:52.917
I'll update you when possible.

13:58.097 --> 14:00.057
It's kinda hard to believe
how much happened

14:00.137 --> 14:03.347
in the short span of time
since we left to meet Perugius.

14:04.187 --> 14:06.937
Nanahoshi collapsed,
we went to the Demon Continent,

14:07.017 --> 14:10.187
met Kishirika,
and pissed off Atofe.

14:10.937 --> 14:12.107
[sighs]

14:12.487 --> 14:14.027
She sure was strong.

14:16.407 --> 14:17.867
And as for me,

14:17.947 --> 14:19.577
I'd better toughen up.

14:20.447 --> 14:21.947
Well, in that regard,

14:22.037 --> 14:24.117
getting a few lessons
from Perugius should be

14:24.207 --> 14:25.957
a move in the right direction.

14:27.417 --> 14:29.997
And... what else was there?

14:31.417 --> 14:34.337
I've got so much to think about
with Mom and Nanahoshi

14:34.417 --> 14:36.297
that I'm forgetting
the older stuff.

14:36.387 --> 14:39.597
If I'm not careful, I'll wind up
repeating old mistakes.

14:40.717 --> 14:42.847
Okay, I'll write it down!

14:42.927 --> 14:44.727
Keeping a diary'll help.

14:44.807 --> 14:46.057
Let's get to writing.

14:46.137 --> 14:47.107
[water splashes]

14:48.017 --> 14:49.607
[scribbling]

14:55.527 --> 14:56.857
[chuckles]

14:58.067 --> 14:58.947
There.

15:03.537 --> 15:06.407
Now then, where do I even start?

15:07.247 --> 15:09.667
How long has it been
since I've kept a diary?

15:10.537 --> 15:13.007
I hope I actually
stick with it this time.

15:23.427 --> 15:24.517
[MAN-GOD] Hi.

15:25.097 --> 15:26.477
[RUDEUS] You again?

15:27.227 --> 15:29.767
Okay, I guess I fell asleep.

15:29.857 --> 15:32.107
-It's been a while, eh?
-It has.

15:32.187 --> 15:34.567
I was off adventuring
for three whole years,

15:34.647 --> 15:36.897
and you never even once
came to visit me.

15:36.987 --> 15:39.907
I mean, I realize I wasn't
always at my best, exactly.

15:39.987 --> 15:41.077
[MAN-GOD] Got that right!

15:41.157 --> 15:42.367
But look at you now!

15:42.447 --> 15:43.737
You've got the wind
in your wings

15:43.827 --> 15:45.787
and seem to be flying
quite high these days.

15:45.867 --> 15:47.247
Well, yeah.

15:47.327 --> 15:49.417
I got married
and have a loving family,

15:49.497 --> 15:51.957
so this is like as far away
from my last life

15:52.037 --> 15:53.547
as you could ever imagine.

15:53.917 --> 15:56.337
You even got to know Perugius,
didn't you?

15:56.417 --> 15:59.177
Oh, Perugius?
He's one of a kind.

15:59.257 --> 16:01.347
And Atofe took a shine to you!

16:01.427 --> 16:03.387
[sighs] Don't remind me.

16:03.467 --> 16:05.217
I wish she had just ignored me.

16:05.727 --> 16:07.057
I would've been in real trouble

16:07.137 --> 16:09.847
if Roxy hadn't taught me
King-class water magic.

16:09.937 --> 16:12.977
True enough. That spell of yours
blew me away.

16:13.057 --> 16:14.227
Yes, indeed.

16:14.517 --> 16:16.607
It's not every day you see
magic ignore battle aura

16:16.687 --> 16:18.567
and paralyze the flesh.

16:18.647 --> 16:21.027
Battle aura? What's that?

16:21.657 --> 16:23.987
Think of it as a way
to use the mana in your body

16:24.077 --> 16:26.117
to boost
your physical abilities.

16:26.657 --> 16:28.997
Once you master it,
you're able to move much faster

16:29.077 --> 16:31.877
and take a lot less damage
than a normal person.

16:32.497 --> 16:34.247
From what I've heard,
it comes naturally

16:34.337 --> 16:36.127
as you continue
to train your body.

16:36.707 --> 16:39.467
I'm in pretty good shape,
but something like that,

16:39.547 --> 16:40.967
I've never felt it.

16:41.587 --> 16:44.677
Some people can't generate aura
no matter how hard they train.

16:44.757 --> 16:46.177
That's just how it works out.

16:46.257 --> 16:48.137
It comes down to talent.

16:48.927 --> 16:50.387
Thanks for the heads up.

16:50.477 --> 16:52.397
Don't let it get you down.

16:52.477 --> 16:55.727
After all, you've got magic
powerful enough to ignore aura.

16:56.267 --> 16:58.067
It should even work on Orsted.

16:58.527 --> 16:59.987
Would it really?

17:00.067 --> 17:02.987
Hey, I don't wanna
start anything with Orsted.

17:03.067 --> 17:04.487
We've got no beef.

17:04.577 --> 17:05.577
Really?

17:06.077 --> 17:09.497
You know, you really helped me
with the Begaritt stuff.

17:10.037 --> 17:12.667
I can't pretend
I don't have any regrets,

17:12.747 --> 17:14.537
but it didn't turn out all bad.

17:15.087 --> 17:17.667
Although I didn't end up
following your advice.

17:17.747 --> 17:20.047
Well, it was your choice,
plain and simple.

17:20.587 --> 17:22.047
[RUDEUS] Just out of curiosity,

17:22.127 --> 17:24.887
what would have happened
if I had chosen not to go?

17:25.347 --> 17:26.637
[MAN-GOD] If you hadn't gone,

17:26.717 --> 17:28.387
your father would've
found a different way

17:28.467 --> 17:32.017
to rescue your mother,
and without dying, no less.

17:32.097 --> 17:33.517
On top of that,
you would've claimed

17:33.597 --> 17:35.517
both beastfolk princesses
for yourself

17:35.607 --> 17:37.727
and lived happily ever after.

17:38.607 --> 17:39.897
You're kidding, right?

17:40.397 --> 17:41.947
Are you telling me
that Paul died

17:42.027 --> 17:43.907
just because I tagged along?

17:43.987 --> 17:45.157
[MAN-GOD] Yes, I am.

17:45.237 --> 17:47.027
It went bad
because you were there,

17:47.117 --> 17:49.117
and he tried
to show off for you.

17:49.617 --> 17:51.577
That's what screwed
the whole thing up.

17:52.207 --> 17:55.127
Yeah, he did, but that can't...

17:55.207 --> 17:57.127
If you had left things alone,

17:57.207 --> 18:00.007
he would have gathered his party
and saved your mother.

18:00.087 --> 18:01.717
And Roxy too, of course.

18:02.507 --> 18:04.887
That's kind of hard to believe.

18:04.967 --> 18:06.797
It's just too good
to be true, you know?

18:07.427 --> 18:08.557
Maybe.

18:08.637 --> 18:11.267
But that's just not
how it works, fate.

18:11.977 --> 18:13.347
Fate, huh?

18:13.437 --> 18:15.937
So, it would've gone
better without me.

18:16.647 --> 18:19.567
God damn it! Hearing that hurts
worse than you know.

18:20.187 --> 18:22.147
[MAN-GOD] It's water
under the bridge.

18:22.687 --> 18:23.857
Guess you're right.

18:24.357 --> 18:25.777
Regret is useless.

18:26.567 --> 18:28.197
Right now, I'm happy.

18:28.277 --> 18:30.157
Maybe I made
the wrong choice then,

18:30.657 --> 18:32.657
but that doesn't change
how things are now.

18:33.867 --> 18:36.247
Truth is, I still
don't think it was all bad.

18:36.667 --> 18:37.837
Not for me.

18:37.917 --> 18:39.797
[MAN-GOD] Ever the optimist.

18:39.877 --> 18:41.757
[RUDEUS] By the way,
why'd you show up now?

18:41.837 --> 18:44.257
Lemme guess, you come
to give me more advice?

18:44.337 --> 18:46.507
[MAN-GOD]
Nah, less like "advice"

18:46.587 --> 18:48.257
and more like "a favor."

18:48.347 --> 18:50.677
[RUDEUS] A favor?
That's a new one.

18:50.767 --> 18:53.307
[MAN-GOD] Even I sometimes
need to call in a favor.

18:54.057 --> 18:55.517
Well, okay.

18:55.597 --> 18:57.057
I've been thinking
it might not hurt

18:57.147 --> 18:58.397
to listen
to what you have to say

18:58.477 --> 19:00.517
and follow your advice
every now and then.

19:00.607 --> 19:02.027
What, really?

19:02.107 --> 19:04.147
It pleases me
to hear you say that!

19:04.237 --> 19:06.857
Look, you've helped me out a ton
throughout this life.

19:06.947 --> 19:09.697
If anything, I'm sorry
I doubted you to begin with.

19:09.777 --> 19:12.237
You do realize I'm a god.

19:12.327 --> 19:13.787
I'd like to think
I'm not in the business

19:13.867 --> 19:15.577
of leading people astray
for fun.

19:15.657 --> 19:17.167
[RUDEUS] Fair point.

19:17.707 --> 19:19.917
So then, what do I need to do?

19:19.997 --> 19:21.417
[MAN-GOD] It's nothing major.

19:22.167 --> 19:24.207
Just go down to your basement

19:24.297 --> 19:26.717
and check it
for anything unusual.

19:26.797 --> 19:30.177
If you don't find anything
down there, then that's that.

19:30.257 --> 19:32.097
Like, unusual how?

19:32.177 --> 19:33.427
And why would I...

19:33.927 --> 19:35.177
Nope, got it.

19:35.557 --> 19:37.347
I won't question you this time.

19:37.437 --> 19:39.267
I'm just gonna
follow your advice.

19:39.357 --> 19:40.517
[Man-God chuckles]

19:40.607 --> 19:41.727
-That so?
-Huh?

19:44.317 --> 19:47.027
[flickering]

19:47.777 --> 19:49.777
[distorted] I appreciate you.

19:55.697 --> 19:56.747
[exhales]

20:00.417 --> 20:02.497
Did Sylphie or Roxy cover me up?

20:02.957 --> 20:05.707
[sighs] Let me come to bed.
Don't leave me.

20:05.797 --> 20:09.427
-[wind whistling]
-[wood clattering]

20:13.057 --> 20:14.467
All right.

20:14.557 --> 20:17.227
[sneezes] Ugh, cold.

20:17.307 --> 20:18.307
Well, they said

20:18.687 --> 20:20.437
that I'm supposed
to check the basement, right?

20:21.307 --> 20:23.017
Weird advice,
but them's the god.

20:23.107 --> 20:24.227
[gasps] Wait,

20:24.567 --> 20:26.397
don't tell me something's
happened to my holy relic.

20:26.857 --> 20:28.487
No, no, no way that's it.

20:29.607 --> 20:30.487
[gasps]

20:35.867 --> 20:37.077
[gasps]

20:41.537 --> 20:42.997
Anyone there?

20:45.587 --> 20:47.297
Reach for the sky!

20:47.797 --> 20:48.967
[chuckles, gasps]

20:51.297 --> 20:52.177
[gasps]

20:53.677 --> 20:56.267
Was I successful?

20:56.927 --> 20:57.967
[gasps]

20:58.057 --> 20:59.017
I see.

20:59.727 --> 21:01.187
I still failed.

21:02.057 --> 21:04.687
Of course.
Why would it have worked?

21:04.767 --> 21:06.187
Who are you?

21:07.647 --> 21:10.197
Are you the Man-God?

21:11.357 --> 21:12.697
[door slams shut]

21:12.777 --> 21:15.077
Don't go to the basement, Rudy.

21:15.487 --> 21:18.577
You were lied to,
deceived by the Man-God.

21:18.657 --> 21:20.497
Slow down, old man.

21:21.157 --> 21:22.667
Who the hell are you?

21:23.167 --> 21:24.667
And how did you get in here?

21:26.127 --> 21:27.207
[OLD MAN] I am...

21:29.877 --> 21:31.417
My name is...

21:31.507 --> 21:35.177
[wind howling]

21:37.057 --> 21:38.637
[RUDEUS] He said

21:38.717 --> 21:41.727
a name that no one
in this world but me would know.

21:42.847 --> 21:46.267
A name that I was going
to take to my grave.

21:47.357 --> 21:49.227
A name I didn't want
to remember,

21:49.727 --> 21:53.067
that belonged to someone
who doesn't exist in this world.

21:53.947 --> 21:57.617
That name was mine
from a previous life.

21:58.237 --> 21:59.487
It's true.

22:00.077 --> 22:01.957
I have come from the future.

22:05.037 --> 22:07.037
[♪ closing theme song playing]
